       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and I know of no indication where 1000 mg/day of sertraline is appropriate. The labeled maximum is 200 mg/day. A tenfold or fivefold error here could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Tell me the dose, such as 100 mg or 200 mg by mouth once daily, and I'll enter it.\n- **Go through pharmacy or the attending.** If an above-range dose is truly intended, for example under a specialist's protocol, it should be reviewed and approved by pharmacy or the attending. They can enter it through the hospital's override process, which usually requires documented justification.\n- **Share the indication.** If you tell me the condition and the rationale, I can help you word the order note for the reviewer. I still wouldn't enter the 1000 mg dose myself."
